  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 AM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nA mid-level ridge centered over the Desert Southwest will remain the \ndominant weather feature through much of the forecast period, \nmaintaining hot and generally dry conditions across South Texas. \nAfternoon temperatures will continue to climb through the week, with \nHeatRisk remaining moderate to major through Friday before moderate \nexpands over most of South Texas to locally extreme across portions \nof the Brush Country over the weekend. Although some locations may \nbriefly meet Heat Advisory criteria on Wednesday, coverage appears \ntoo limited for an advisory at this time. Please continue to \npractice heat safety as heat indices around 110 and higher become \nincreasingly common this week, especially this weekend with isolated \nlocations across the southern Coastal Bend approaching 118 degrees.\n\nForecast confidence decreases slightly late Saturday into Sunday as \na weak mid-level disturbance rounds the eastern periphery of the \nridge, bringing a low (15-20%) chance around the Victoria Crossroads \nfor showers and thunderstorms with most locations expected to remain \nhot and dry.",
